d #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{50(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402281} {:answer/id #uuid "c0f34d3a-cfa0-5e02-8320-e125baa30770" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{50(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402282} {:answer/id #uuid "4a7ac352-d46a-51ed-a992-d68e07a53b35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{250(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a7ac352-d46a-51ed-a992-d68e07a53b35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{250(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402283} :answer-field/id #uuid "c69873a9-e21f-55cc-ba65-c7ed6f009b57" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de25ec60-135e-5b0f-93ec-2a89a92381de" :question/math-academy-id "q-343341" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $10$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=5x$ defined on $[-5,5).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of a series converging to the $10$-periodic extension of \n\n$$\nG(x)=\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}={\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n5x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{50(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}} \non $R,$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an odd function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=5$ and we are already given the coefficients ${b}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{50(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the function $F$ is continuous on $(-5,5).$ \nTherefore, the $10$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{piecewise continuous}$ on $R,$ so we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}5t\\,\\text{d}t & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{50(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi t}{5})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ {[\\frac{5}{2}{t}^{2}]}_{0}^{x} & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{50(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\cdot [-\\frac{5}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi t}{5})]_{0}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2} & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{250(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5}))\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402302 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f6f980b-262a-50f0-ae3d-21301e83956a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1)^{n+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402304} {:answer/id #uuid "c9091f78-a863-5b79-82af-d78f1b7a6e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402305} {:answer/id #uuid "ff2405a2-3755-5df5-98e5-3e6b5d35f747" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402306} {:answer/id #uuid "81d46c72-93bb-5c34-b05d-8f8e24f569a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1)^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81d46c72-93bb-5c34-b05d-8f8e24f569a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860